There are six reasons for the difficulty of flaring off of diesel generator sets, one of which is that the solenoid valve is not closed strictly. News
Why is that?
The shutdown solenoid valve is not closed strictly, in addition to processing reasons, and the cleanliness of the fuel also has a great relationship. When the fuel cleanliness is low, impurities will intrude into the solenoid valve, the valve pad up or make its movement card lag, resulting in lax closure; Impurities may also be in the maintenance process do not pay attention to the cleaning of the oil pipeline and direct invasion.
Because the solenoid valve is not closed strictly and caused by flutter out difficult, often can increase the throttle to impact the valve sheet, so that it closes the oil circuit and the engine immediately flutter. After the fault occurs, the solenoid valve should be cleaned to eliminate, but the most important thing is to improve the cleanliness of the fuel, otherwise the fault will occur repeatedly.
